# CUTLY knowledge docs

Canonical docs live at the repo root: `PRD.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `DESIGN.md`, `RULES.md`, `TASKS.md`, `MEMORY.md`.

## When to update (same session as the code change)

| Change type | Update |
| --- | --- |
| New/changed user-facing flow, audience, or non-goal | `PRD.md` |
| Routes, API, schema, session/auth, deploy/host | `ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| Tokens, tab bar, setup/auth UI patterns, motion | `DESIGN.md` |
| Process, invariants, agent constraints | `RULES.md` |
| Work started, finished, or newly scoped | `TASKS.md` (move `[ ]` / `[x]`) |
| Env quirks, locked decisions, pitfalls, test data | `MEMORY.md` (dated note) |
| Customer-side (CJ-*) booking/explore/pay change | **Also** append/update `TASKS.md` → **Partner setup — later backlog (PS-*)** with what partner setup / Floor / Profile must add or modify |

## How

- Edit only the sections that changed; keep docs concise.
- Do not invent future features into PRD as “done”.
- Prefer these six over stale `docs/PROJECT_INDEX.md`.
- If the user asks for a feature that contradicts MEMORY/PRD, surface the conflict briefly before coding.
- **Partner mirror (always):** When shipping or scoping a customer journey fix, add a `PS-*` row (or mark an existing one) so partner-side work is never forgotten. Do not block the customer fix on building PS-* unless the user asks.
